The request names its own host, and nothing else does.

Forwarded and X-Forwarded-Host are client-controlled unless the application has
an explicit trusted-proxy boundary, and this one has none. Composery's supported
edges - Caddy, the cloud proxy - preserve Host, so Host is the single authority
for origin checks and port-domain routing.

The workbench drops X-Forwarded-Prefix for the same reason. Its relative-URL
calculation already derives every browser path from the request URL, so the
header fallback was both unreachable and a second authority a client could
write. The constructor slot stays positional for VS Code's instantiation helper
but is no longer stored as state.

